==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|hæmophilia}}
* {{l|en|hemophilia}}

===Etymology===
Medical term; {{confix|haemo|philia|lang=en}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} [[αἷμα]] ([[blood]]) + [[φιλία]] ([[friendship]])

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɪliə|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|British spelling|pathology}} Any of several hereditary illnesses that impair the body's ability to control bleeding, usually passed from mother to son.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|bleeder's disease}}
* {{l|en|Christmas disease}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|haemophiliac}}
* {{l|en|haemophilic}}
* {{l|en|haemophile}}

